PROPOSED. Not applied on this branch: src/lib/esign.server.ts is pinned to the
published branch by scripts/agreement-evidence.test.cjs, so changing it needs
explicit Owner approval (and that pin updated in the same reviewed change).

Why: M2 step 19 (private.finalized_archive_document_v1) forbids moving a finalized
eSign document, and private.bind_document_integrity_v1 binds only the address
immutable-v1/<document>/<sha256>.pdf. So the eSign v1 archive (behind
SIGNED_ARCHIVE_V1_ENABLED, still false) must write the completed PDF straight to
that address; Record Rental then binds it in place. Without this, no new eSign
agreement can become Record Rental evidence. Live behaviour is unchanged while the
flag stays false. The two eSign archive tests are updated to the new layout; with
the patch applied they pass (36/36). The acceptance test's new-renter fixture
writes exactly what this produces.

Apply: git apply proposed/record-rental-historical/03-esign-immutable-v1-archive.patch

